<http://data.silknow.org/object/988e4f91-6a45-3a1a-9581-b21d1e38cc01/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Tapestry produced by Charles Sallandrouze de Lamornaix after a  design by Jean-Baptiste Amedee  Couder, Aubusson, France, 1855.\n\nThis tapestry has been woven in wool and silk on cotton, and showes an allegory of  America. In the centre foreground a snake rears above a chest of jewels  is surrounded by fruits and flowers.  Behind are draped two flags, one is  the Star and Stripes of which only a  part is visible, and the Flag of the  Republic of Haiti with a central  device of a palm tree surmounted by  a Cap of Liberty.  Exotic birds and  insects fly among the background  plants, cactus and a type of palm  tree."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/988e4f91-6a45-3a1a-9581-b21d1e38cc01> .

